\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Love of love, and light of light,
\par Heavenly Father all maintaining;
\par Wisdom hid in highest height,
\par To Thy creature fondly deigning;
\par Maker wonderful and just,
\par Thou hast call'd my heart to trust.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. What are life's unnumber'd cares,
\par Sorrow, torment, passing measure?
\par O'er my short-lived pains and fears
\par Surely ruleth Thy good pleasure.
\par Boundless is Thy love for me,
\par Boundless then my trust shall be.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Every burden weigheth light,
\par Since in Thee my hope abideth:
\par Sweetly bright my darkest night,
\par While on Thee my mind confideth.
\par Give Thy gift, I Thee implore,
\par Thee to trust for evermore.
\par                             Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

